---
import SaidDocsLayout from "../../../layouts/SaidDocsLayout.astro";
import SaidShot from "../../../components/SaidShot.astro";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  name: "Set up Said and Done: first boot to first board",
  description:
    "Install Said and Done, point it at your notes folder, pick its face, and land on a working board.",
  step: [
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Install Said and Done" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Point it at your notes folder" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Pick the board or the dossier" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Answer the phone-home question" },
    { "@type": "HowToStep", name: "Make the first card" },
  ],
};
---

<SaidDocsLayout
  title="First boot, first board — Said and Done guides"
  description="Install Said and Done, point it at your notes folder, pick its face, and land on a working board — in about two minutes."
  section="guides"
  kicker="Guide 01"
  heading="First boot, first board"
  dek="About three minutes, one folder decision."
  slug="first-boot"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    Said and Done arrives whole: the installer carries everything it needs, and nothing
    is downloaded at boot. Your only real decision is which folder holds your
    notes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">1 · Install</h2>
  <p>
    Run the installer for your platform. On Linux it installs to your own user,
    puts <code>said</code> on your path, and adds the launcher entry. On macOS you
    drag Said and Done to Applications. On Windows it installs per-user with a normal uninstaller.
    No elevation, no system folders — and uninstalling never touches your data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="notes">2 · Point it at your notes</h2>
  <p>
    First boot asks one thing first: where do your notes live? Walk to the
    folder that holds your work and take it. Every folder inside becomes a
    project; nothing is copied or moved. No notes folder yet? Take the suggested
    fresh one and grow into it.
  </p>
  <SaidShot
    src="/said-and-done/shots/wizard-folder.png"
    alt="The first-boot folder picker, walking the home folder"
  />

  <h2 id="face">3 · Pick its face</h2>
  <p>
    Choose how the desk opens: <strong>the board</strong>, where lanes carry
    cards left to right — or <strong>the dossier</strong>, one running record
    with the freshest word on top. Both previews animate live while you decide,
    and Settings can always change your mind later.
  </p>
  <SaidShot
    src="/said-and-done/shots/wizard-face.png"
    alt="The face chooser — the board and the dossier previews, side by side"
  />

  <h2 id="questions">4 · One honest question</h2>
  <p>
    May Said and Done send crash reports home? Yes or no — and Settings can change your
    mind later. That's the whole interview.
  </p>

  <h2 id="first-card">5 · The first card</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Press <code>n</code> — a new card opens.</li>
    <li>Give it a title in your own words.</li>
    <li>Press <code>enter</code> — it lands in the lane, numbered for life.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    That's the whole loop. Say it, move it, and when it's finished — mark it
    done. <strong>Said and Done.</strong>
  </p>
</SaidDocsLayout>
